	)
	(text "Notes:\n1 - I have used AMS1117-3.3 voltage redulator. \nThe circiut is copied as in the datasheet.\n\n2 - Maybe use 4u7 capacitors as well to decrease \nthe Bill of Materials. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.494 171.704 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3cd1c9d6-b4d2-45b9-a9aa-621e0df73567")
	)
	(text "Notes:\n1 - Ihave connected the 3.3V to the ESP with capacitors to stabize the 3.3V. They are decoupling capacitors. \n\n2 - All the pins are labeled via global labels.\n\n3 - Two buttons are added. One above is enable button. Some applications shows that we can connect enable button to directly GND via capacitors.\n\n4- Second button is BOOT button. In order for the Chip Boot Mode, strapping pins GPIO0 and GPIO2 should pulled down."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.952 128.524 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4b2777ea-804f-4201-83ae-3edab2f12dc1")
	)
	(text "Notes:\n1 - I have used PESD5V0L1ULD for esd. But in our stock we have BAT54C. \nI have search for it but i did not understand. How may we implement that component?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.748 110.998 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67ce46e3-c797-4ef8-9b00-17e3aaf7e45c")
	)
